  "result": "Fixed. `#` inside an argument no longer truncates the completion input.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex` with its default `commenters='#'`. Any `#` that starts a word or appears mid-word is treated as a shell comment, so the rest of the line is dropped. For example, `cli a#b` became `['cli', 'a']`, and `cli #x y` became `['cli']`.\n\n**Change:**\n- `src/click/shell_completion.py`: set `lex.commenters = \"\"` (with a short comment), which is what `shlex.split` does when comments are disabled.\n- `tests/test_parser.py`: added three cases: `cli a#b`, `cli #x y`, and `cli 'a#b'`. I confirmed the first two produce the wrong output with the old shlex behavior.\n\n**Verification:** `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (68 tests). The full suite gives 1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, with no failures.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. The top section is already released (8.5.0), and I didn't want to guess at the next version or issue number. Let me know if you want one added under a new unreleased heading.",
